  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Security Risks and Natural Resources Management to Safeguard Human Mobility and Peaceful Co-existence in Central Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This joint IOM-UNDP project will aim to contribute to reducing competition between communities over natural resources while strengthening their climate resilience through adaptive capacity targeted at environmental preservation and finally to better analyze and understand climate-related conflicts in order to enable more effective prevention actions. The proposed approach implies that if the direct and indirect impacts of climate change are identified, if the frequency and nature of related conflicts are known, if the prevention and management capacities of local authorities and communities are strengthened, then the climate resilience and security of the populations of the north and center can be improved through the implementation of high-impact actions, based on evidence and lessons learned from empirical experiences. Furthermore, if local options and mechanisms for prevention and adaptation to climate change are known, then it would be easier to support central and local authorities as well as civil society actors in a youth and women-centered approach to addressing climate security challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
